Section 1: Campus Health Frameworks & Policy Guidance
HIGHER HEALTH National Framework
HIGHER HEALTH (the Higher Education and Training Health, Wellness and Development Centre) is the dedicated agency established by the South African Department of Higher Education and Training (DHET) to manage health and wellness across 420+ public university and TVET campus sites nationwide. Its primary mandates include:
Comprehensive Student Health Standard: Standardized delivery of primary healthcare, sexual and reproductive health (SRH), HIV/TB/STI prevention and management, gender-based violence (GBV) support, and mental health interventions across higher education institutions.
24/7 Crisis Helpline: Centralized national telephonic counselling and crisis response line (0800 36 36 36) linked directly to regional student support centers.
Peer Educator Framework: Peer-to-peer wellness programs designed to build resilience, decrease stigma around mental health, and provide early detection and referral.
