1. Clinical Governance & Practitioner Registration
All medical practitioners, clinical nurse practitioners (CNPs), and psychologists are registered with the Health Professions Council of South Africa (HPCSA).
Social workers and peer counsellors operate under the South African Council for Social Service Professions (SACSSP).
Pharmacy operations adhere strictly to the rules of the South African Pharmacy Council (SAPC) and the Medicines and Related Substances Act (Act 101 of 1965).
2. Key Policies, SOPs, and Operational Flowcharts
UCT Student Mental Health Policy: Employs a stepped-care model. Interventions range from low-intensity self-management (apps like Panda and Vimbo, peer support programs) to medium-intensity individual/group psychotherapy, up to high-intensity psychiatric crisis intervention.
SOP Crisis Intervention & Psychiatric Emergencies Flowchart:
Office Hours (08:30–16:00): Triage via the SWS Hotline (021 650 1020) or the Ivan Toms Building emergency intake.
After Hours & Emergency Response: Immediate escalation to UCT Campus Protection Services (CPS: 080 650 2222), UCT Careline (0800 24 25 26 operated by SADAG), or SWS Psychiatric Emergency Line (021 650 1271).
Hospital Transfers: Partnered emergency centers include Groote Schuur Hospital (Public Tertiary), Rondebosch Medical Centre (Private, via SWS pre-approval), and Life Claremont / Vincent Pallotti Hospitals.
Communicable Diseases & Infection Prevention Protocol: Follows Guidance on Management of Communicable Diseases (GMCD). Defines protocols for isolation, screening, and outbreak management for Tuberculosis (TB), Influenza, COVID-19, and Chickenpox.
Confidentiality Framework: Strict medical confidentiality under HPCSA/SACSSP codes. Personal health data cannot be shared with university academic faculties or external parties without written student consent, except under statutory exemptions:
Express written consent by the student.
Imminent risk to the life or physical safety of the student or others.
Court order / subpoena.
Internal multidisciplinary case management within SWS (bounded by clinical confidentiality).
