1. Booking & Scheduling Engine
Multi-Role Scheduling: Differentiates between Clinical Nurse Practitioners (CNPs - zero consultation fee), Medical Doctors (fee/medical aid billed), Psychologists/Counselors, and Pharmacy Repeat Collection slots.
Intelligent Triage Filtering: Before confirming an appointment, students complete a digital symptom checker. High-risk responses (e.g., severe suicidal ideation, chest pain, acute dyspnea) bypass routine booking and trigger the Crisis Protocol (displaying instant emergency call buttons and alerting the SWS triage nurse dashboard).
Slot Management: Supports walk-in triage buffers, online advance booking, and automated cancellation/rescheduling windows (requiring 2-hour notice to optimize slot utilization).
2. Electronic Health Record (EHR) & Clinical Encounter Management
Student Identity Verification: Synchronizes with campus LDAP/Active Directory to fetch verified Student ID, full legal name, date of birth, and home department.
SOAP Documentation Workflow:
Subjective: Chief complaint, history of present illness (HPI), allergy flags, social history.
Objective: Vital signs (BP, HR, SpO2, Temp, Glucose), physical exam findings.
Assessment: Primary and secondary ICD-10 diagnostic codes.
Plan: e-Prescriptions, lab requisitions, referral notes, and follow-up directives.
Multidisciplinary Case Notes: Encrypted notes visible only to assigned care team members (GP, Psychologist, Pharmacist) with granular permission levels.
3. Pharmacy Dispensing & Chronic Medication System
e-Prescription Routing: Doctors and CNPs submit structured prescriptions directly to the internal pharmacy queue in real time.
Pharmacist Dispensing Workflow:
Verification against drug interaction databases and allergy history.
SAPC Schedule 1 to Schedule 6 drug ledger tracking.
Batch number logging and expiration tracking.
Repeat Chronic Medication Lifecycle: Automated monthly re-authorization, SMS/WhatsApp notification when chronic packs are prepared, and secure QR-code-based pickup validation at the SWS pharmacy window or automated collection lockers.
4. Follow-Up & Care Continuum Engine
Automated Communication Pipeline:
Appointment reminders sent 24 hours and 2 hours prior via SMS/Email/WhatsApp.
Post-consultation care instructions and feedback surveys.
Missed Appointment (No-Show) Protocol:
Routine Primary Care: Sends an automated rescheduling link.
High-Risk Mental Health: Flags the student on the SWS Social Work/Peer Support dashboard to trigger a proactive wellness call or escalation.
5. Privacy, Compliance & Data Architecture Standards
Standard / Law	Mandatory System Controls & Architecture Requirements
POPIA (South Africa)	
• Health records categorized as Special Personal Information (Sec 26 & 32).


• Explicit, granular consent management for processing and internal sharing.


• Automated audit trail logging every view, edit, export, or deletion.


• Support for Data Subject Access Rights (Data access, correction, and deletion requests).

HIPAA (International)	
• AES-256 encryption at rest; TLS 1.3 encryption in transit.


• Strict Role-Based & Attribute-Based Access Controls (RBAC/ABAC).


• Immutable access logs storing timestamp, user ID, IP address, and record ID.

HL7 FHIR R4	
Standardized JSON payload models across all RESTful API endpoints:


• Patient: Student identity and demographics.


• Practitioner: Healthcare provider details and HPCSA registration.


• Appointment / Slot: Scheduling state machine.


• Encounter: Individual clinical visit session.


• Condition / Observation: Diagnostic codes (ICD-10) and vital signs.


• MedicationRequest / MedicationDispense: Prescription & pharmacy dispensing logic.
